WEBVTT

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.920
(UPBEAT JAZZ PLAYING)

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.200
(ROARS)

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.720
(WOMAN SHRIEKS)

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:00.560
(SQUEAKING)

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.960
MOTHER: Good night, sweetheart.
BOY: 'Night, Mom.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.080
MAN: Sleep tight, kiddo.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.080
(DOOR CLOSES)

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:42.760
(OWL HOOTING)

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.520
(DOOR CREAKING)

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.000
(GASPS)

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.520
(GURGLING SNARL)

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.360
(SCREAMING)

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.960
(SCREAMING LOUDER)

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:53.960
Whoa!

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.880
(SHRIEKING)

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.000
(SCREAMING)

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.680
Oh! Aye! Oh! Oh!

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.400
(ALARM BLARING)

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.520
COMPUTER VOICE:
Simulation terminated.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:22.520
-All right. Mr. Bile, is it?
-My friends call me Phlegm.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.200
Mr. Bile, can you tell me
what you did wrong?

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:29.520
-I fell down?
-No, no, before that.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.920
Can anyone tell me
Mr. Bile's big mistake?

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:34.920
Anyone?

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.000
(COUGHS)

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.040
(GROANS)

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.960
Let's take a look at the tape.
Here we go.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.880
Right there.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.040
See? The door.
You left it wide open.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.560
(ALL MURMURING)

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:49.520
And leaving the door open
is the worst mistake

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.440
any employee can make because...

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:57.720
-It could let in a draft?
-WATERNOOSE: It could let in a child.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.200
Oh! Mr. Waternoose.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.080
There's nothing more toxic or deadly
than a human child.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.320
A single touch could kill you.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.480
Leave a door open and a child
could walk right into this factory,

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.200
right into the monster world.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.760
I won't go in a kid's room.
You can't make me.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.000
You're going in there
because we need this.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.200
(ALL SCREAMING)

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.440
(WHIMPERING)

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.600
(STATIC)

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:30.720
Our city is counting on you
to collect those children's screams.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.600
Without scream we have no power.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.760
Yes, it's dangerous work.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.480
And that's why I need you
to be at your best.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:42.600
I need scarers who are
confident, tenacious, tough.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.440
Intimidating.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.920
I need scarers like...
Like James P. Sullivan.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:51.800
(SNORING)

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:57.240
MIKE: Hey, good morning,
Monstropolis. It's five after 6:00 a.m.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.080
in the big Monster City.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:02.840
The temperature's a balmy 65 degrees
which is good for you reptiles.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:06.960
And it looks like it's gonna be
a perfect day to lie in bed, sleep in,

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:11.640
or simply work off that flab
that's hanging over the bed!

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:12.960
Get up, Sulley!

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.280
(GASPING)

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.920
I don't believe I ordered
a wake-up call, Mikey.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.280
Less talk, more pain,
marshmallow boy!

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.320
(GROWLS)

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.000
Feel the burn.
You call yourself a monster?

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.600
Scary feet, scary feet.
The kid's awake!

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:29.360
Scary feet, scary feet, scary feet.
Kid's asleep!

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:31.960
Twins! In a bunk bed!

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.400
(GROWLING)

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.760
I thought I had you there.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:39.840
OK, Sulley, here we go.
You ready? Follow it. It's over here.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:43.480
Over there. Don't let the kid touch you.
Don't let him touch you!

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.960
♪ I don't know but it's been said
I love scarin' kids in bed ♪

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.440
Fight that plaque.
Scary monsters don't have plaque.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:52.840
One-eighteen. Do you have 119?

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.560
Do I see 120?

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.360
-I don't believe it.
-I'm not breaking a sweat.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.760
Not you. Look!
The new commercial's on.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:03.880
ANNOUNCER: The future is bright
at Monsters, Incorporated.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:06.160
-I'm in this one.
-ANNOUNCER: We're part of your life.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.040
We power your car.
We warm your home.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:10.800
We light your city.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:13.360
-I'm Monsters, Incorporated.
-Hey, look! Betty!

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:17.320
Carefully matching every child
to their ideal monster,

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:19.440
to produce superior scream.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.400
ANNOUNCER: Refined into clean,
dependable energy.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:26.960
Every time you turn something on,
Monsters, Incorporated is there.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:28.920
I'm Monsters, Incorporated.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.720
ANNOUNCER: We know the challenge.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:32.320
The window of innocence is shrinking.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:35.040
Human kids are harder to scare.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.720
Of course,
MI is prepared for the future.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.040
With the top scarers,

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.680
the best refineries,

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.320
and research into
new energy techniques.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.400
(SCREAMING)

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:46.560
OK, here I come.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.680
We're working for a better tomorrow,

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:50.760
today.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:53.520
WORKERS:
We're Monsters, Incorporated.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.400
ANNOUNCER: We're MI,
Monsters, Incorporated.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.760
We scare because we care.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.040
-I can't believe it.
-Mike.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:05.400
I was on TV!

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.280
Did you see me? I'm a natural.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:08.320
(PHONE RINGS)

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.040
Hello?
I know! Wasn't I great?

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.720
Did the whole family see it?
It's your mom.

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.680
What can I say?
The camera loves me.

